WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.960
– [Zac] Jamie Lloyd was born in late 1980 or early to&nbsp;
mid 1981. We know this because Jamie is first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:09.600
introduced to us at 4am on October 31st in&nbsp;
1988, where she is referred to as being seven&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:13.520
years old. Jamie’s mother was Laurie Strode&nbsp;
and her father was a man with the last name&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.520 --> 00:00:16.400
Lloyd… and that’s pretty much all that’s pretty&nbsp;
much all we ever learn about him. Jamie had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:19.920
what seems like a pretty happy childhood for&nbsp;
the first seven years of her life. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:23.440
in November of 1987, her mother and&nbsp;
father are killed in an accident.

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:24.720
– I know you miss your&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:28.560
parents. It hasn’t been that long.
– It’s been eleven months.

00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:31.920
– Jamie was adopted by Darlene and Richard&nbsp;
Carruthers, who knew Jamie’s family&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:35.440
because Laurie once babysat for their own&nbsp;
daughter, Rachel, who is now a teenager.

00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:38.960
Jamie clings to her new adoptive sister –&nbsp;
a similarity she shares with Andy Barclay&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:42.080
from Child’s Play, who I’ve talked about&nbsp;
on a previous episode of Horror History.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.080 --> 00:00:44.400
Jamie pleads with Rachel to&nbsp;
love her like a real sister,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:48.640
as she tries to find where she fits in with her&nbsp;new
adopted family. While Rachel and Jamie do form&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:52.160
a special bond, their time together&nbsp;
would quite literally be cut short.

00:00:52.160 --> 00:00:54.880
To find out more about why Jamie&nbsp;
copes the way she does with the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.880 --> 00:00:58.600
trauma caused by her Uncle -- Haddonfield&nbsp;
boogeyman Michael Myers -- and the long&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.600 --> 00:01:02.240
term psychological effects he causes,&nbsp;
stick around to the end of this video.

00:01:02.715 --> 00:01:04.845
(metal music)

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:14.240
Welcome to Horror History. Jamie Lloyd does not&nbsp;
need an unstoppable killing machine to come after&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:18.080
her in order to gain some psychological&nbsp;
issues. When we first meet her character,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.080 --> 00:01:21.440
played by the then unknown actress Danielle&nbsp;
Harris, she is struggling to cope with the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.440 --> 00:01:25.840
recent loss of her parents, and, perhaps&nbsp;
as a result, suffers chronic insomnia.

00:01:25.840 --> 00:01:31.920
– [Rachel] Kiddo. It’s four in the morning.
– [Jamie] I can’t sleep.

00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:35.920
– What is this, four nights in a row?&nbsp;
Are you going for a record here? The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.920 --> 00:01:38.160
seven year old insomniac’s hall of fame?

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:41.600
– Despite Rachel trivializing the mental&nbsp;
illness of an innocent agonized orphan,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:45.840
according to The Child Mind Institute; “symptoms&nbsp;
of trauma in children closely mimic depression,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:50.240
including too much or too little sleep.” That&nbsp;
probably explains Jamie’s difficulty with sleep,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.240 --> 00:01:53.840
but her issues may go deeper than what&nbsp;
meets the eye. To understand her behavior,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.840 --> 00:01:57.040
we also need to analyze her mother,&nbsp;
Laurie Strode, so let’s take it back&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.040 --> 00:02:04.924
to that fateful Halloween night in 1978,&nbsp;
when Laurie was take- en-to-the hos-pit-al.

00:02:04.924 --> 00:02:07.308
(mysterious music)

00:02:09.280 --> 00:02:12.000
As I mentioned in my Things You&nbsp;
Missed episode on Halloween II,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:14.080
Laurie has a deep seated fear of going to sleep,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.080 --> 00:02:17.680
which I interpreted as her subconscious&nbsp;
being scared to dream about Michael Myers.

00:02:17.680 --> 00:02:21.840
Just like Laurie, Jamie avoids sleeping&nbsp;
due in part to her own fear of nightmares&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.840 --> 00:02:25.120
involving Michael. After being convinced&nbsp;
to go to bed by Rachel in the early hours&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.120 --> 00:02:28.640
of the morning on Halloween, Jamie suffers&nbsp;
from nightmares of Michael coming after her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.640 --> 00:02:32.240
in her room. Although they have never&nbsp;
met, Jamie already knows what the adult Michael&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.240 --> 00:02:35.920
Myers looks like. It’s almost as if her&nbsp;
mother’s trauma was passed down to her.

00:02:35.920 --> 00:02:39.840
We don’t know how Laurie and Jamie’s father raised&nbsp;
their child. They may have shielded her from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:43.680
finding out about the horrible crimes her uncle&nbsp;
committed, or they may have done the opposite&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:48.000
and tried to warn her and teach her about him,&nbsp;
with concern that he could one day escape again.

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:51.360
Jamie is part of the original Halloween&nbsp;
timeline, but Laurie also has a kid&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.360 --> 00:02:54.800
both in the 20 and 40 year timelines.&nbsp;
Because those are different continuities,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.800 --> 00:02:57.760
they are essentially different versions&nbsp;
of the Laurie Strode character, but if&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.760 --> 00:03:01.760
this Laurie is anything like those Lauries she&nbsp;
would have prepared Jamie for Michael’s return.

00:03:01.760 --> 00:03:04.720
In fact, in the 40 year timeline,&nbsp;
Laurie has a daughter named Karen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.720 --> 00:03:08.560
who she trains to use firearms and is&nbsp;
extremely strict with in regards to her safety.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.560 --> 00:03:12.640
Rumor has it that in the original script of&nbsp;
Halloween (2018), Karen’s name was Jamie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.640 --> 00:03:15.760
as if she were an alternate version&nbsp;
of Jamie Lloyd. I guess in the end,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.760 --> 00:03:18.880
they were worried that this would be&nbsp;
too confusing so she’s now a Karen.

00:03:19.352 --> 00:03:21.172
– [Karen] Hey mom... I thought you quit drinking?

00:03:21.172 --> 00:03:21.672
(Laurie grunts)

00:03:21.672 --> 00:03:23.512
– [Karen] This is exactly why we don't reach out.

00:03:23.600 --> 00:03:27.440
– But back to our Jamie. If her mother wasn’t&nbsp;
the one to inform her about Michael Myers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:31.040
her classmates made sure she knew about&nbsp;
her embarrassing family connection.

00:03:31.040 --> 00:03:35.200
– [Jamie] I don’t need to wear a stupid costume.
– [Boy] That’s because every day is Halloween at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:38.831
Jamie’s house! Right, Jamie? Because&nbsp;
your uncle’s the boogeyman! 

00:03:38.831 --> 00:03:42.853
– [Students] (chanting in unison) Boogeyman! Boogeyman! Jamie's uncle's a boogeyman!

00:03:42.934 --> 00:03:46.291
– [Girl] How come your Mommy didn’t make&nbsp;
you a costume, Jamie?

00:03:46.291 --> 00:03:47.760
– [Boy] How could she? Her Mom is dead!

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:49.120
(meme laugh)

00:03:49.120 --> 00:03:52.640
– Jamie runs away trying to stifle what looks&nbsp;
like a panic attack. When Rachel picks her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.640 --> 00:03:56.000
up from school, with her friend Lindsey, they&nbsp;
drive to get some ice-cream. Jamie expresses&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.000 --> 00:04:00.160
that she now wants to participate in Halloween,&nbsp;
where she had not shown any previous interest.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.160 --> 00:04:05.280
Oh good, we don’t have to slit her throat. It’s&nbsp;
clear that Jamie wants to fit in with the other&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.280 --> 00:04:09.520
kids. Rachel takes her to buy a Halloween costume&nbsp;
and she chooses a clown costume, very similar to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.520 --> 00:04:13.840
the one Michael wore as he stabbed his sister&nbsp;
Judith, when he was Jamie’s age in the 60s.

00:04:13.840 --> 00:04:17.520
Jamie looks in the mirror to admire the&nbsp;
costume but instead she sees Michael Myers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:20.640
in her reflection. Jamie is aware of what&nbsp;
Michael looked like as a child, because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.640 --> 00:04:24.320
she has a shoebox at home full of old photos,&nbsp;
which not only includes pictures of her Mom,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.320 --> 00:04:28.000
but also this shot of the prepubescent&nbsp;
Michael, which is more evidence that Laurie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:31.760
probably did tell her the truth about her uncle.&nbsp;
As she starts to hyperventilate and panic,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.760 --> 00:04:35.040
she turns around to see the adult&nbsp;
Michael Myers standing behind her.

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:38.720
She freaks out, getting the attention of&nbsp;
everyone around her and Michael disappears.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:38.720 --> 00:04:42.880
Rachel tries to comfort Jamie as they leave. We&nbsp;
never actually see them pay for the costume, so,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.880 --> 00:04:45.360
I guess Rachel and Jamie are just shoplifters now.

00:04:45.360 --> 00:04:49.120
Darlene and Richard go out that evening, leaving&nbsp;
Rachel to take Jamie trick-or-treating. She&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.120 --> 00:04:51.920
actually makes peace with some of the kids&nbsp;
that were picking on her at school and ends&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.920 --> 00:04:54.960
up joining their group. They arrive at the&nbsp;
Meekers’ house, where they’re greeted by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.960 --> 00:04:58.320
Rachel’s classmate, Kelly Meeker, wearing&nbsp;
only her Cops Do It By The Book Shirt,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.320 --> 00:05:02.320
which I’m gonna put on over my clothes right now&nbsp;
because I need more excuses to wear this thing.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.320 --> 00:05:06.240
Rachel gets upset when she sees the boy she’s&nbsp;
interested in, Brady, emerge from the hallway,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.240 --> 00:05:10.640
making it clear that they were probably hooking&nbsp;
up. As Rachel storms off in a fit of JGS,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.640 --> 00:05:14.640
Brady chases after her, but Jamie doesn’t&nbsp;
realize and continues on with her new friends.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:14.640 --> 00:05:20.000
She soon finds herself separated; lost on&nbsp;
Halloween night with a killer on the loose.

00:05:20.170 --> 00:05:23.438
(cinematic impact)

00:05:25.242 --> 00:05:28.193
(ominous guitar music)

00:05:29.040 --> 00:05:32.640
As trick-or-treaters vacate the streets,&nbsp;
Rachel and Jamie try to find each other.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.640 --> 00:05:36.480
Jamie thinks she’s being followed, but luckily&nbsp;
for her, Rachel finds her and the Haddonfield&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.480 --> 00:05:40.160
police find both of them just in time.&nbsp;
As they pull away, they’re surrounded by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.160 --> 00:05:44.480
pranksters dressed up as Michael Myers, which&nbsp;
seems to be a Darwin Award waiting to happen.

00:05:44.480 --> 00:05:45.655
– [Dr. Loomis] Dear God.

00:05:45.655 --> 00:05:48.160
(Draws his gun)
– Hey, don’t shoot!

00:05:48.160 --> 00:05:52.160
– While it seems as if no damage is done this&nbsp;
time, for Jamie, who is already struggling to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:52.160 --> 00:05:56.960
decipher what’s real and what’s a dream, this only&nbsp;
leaves her feeling more scared and confused.

00:05:56.960 --> 00:06:00.080
After discovering that the police station&nbsp;
has already been ravaged by Michael Myers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.080 --> 00:06:04.160
Sheriff Meeker takes Jamie, Rachel and Dr.&nbsp;
Loomis to his own house for safety. Jamie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:04.160 --> 00:06:07.520
is ushered upstairs to get some rest and&nbsp;
Rachel tries to comfort her. At some point,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.520 --> 00:06:10.880
Jamie does appear to fall asleep, so&nbsp;
Rachel heads downstairs to investigate.&nbsp;

00:06:10.880 --> 00:06:14.320
The sheriff assigns an officer to keep watch at&nbsp;
the front door, and Loomis leaves to go back to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.320 --> 00:06:17.760
Jamie’s house, hoping he can catch Michael&nbsp;
Myers there. The Sheriff gets word that the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:17.760 --> 00:06:21.600
local Illinois boys from the bar accidentally&nbsp;
killed a guy and leaves to address this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:21.600 --> 00:06:25.840
so Jamie’s life is now in the hands of a bunch&nbsp;
of teenagers and a single police officer.

00:06:25.840 --> 00:06:30.000
Noises downstairs wake her up, and she&nbsp;
realizes Rachel is gone, which discomforts her,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:33.760
and she comes out of the upstairs bedroom just&nbsp;
in time to her adoptive sister rushing back to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:33.760 --> 00:06:38.640
her in a panic, which is a relief until she&nbsp;
realizes that Michael Myers isn’t far behind.

00:06:38.640 --> 00:06:41.440
She actually witnesses Brady’s&nbsp;
head getting literally ripped off,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:41.440 --> 00:06:43.840
as if there wasn’t enough&nbsp;
for her to be traumatized by.

00:06:43.840 --> 00:06:48.015
– [Announcer] “Here comes the&nbsp;
rush and here’s the hit; OH!”

00:06:48.015 --> 00:06:52.240
– Uhh, not that Brady. Jamie and Rachel are chased&nbsp;
into the attic and they’re able to escape to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:52.240 --> 00:06:56.640
roof, but Michael follows them, and the only way&nbsp;
she’s able to get away is John McClane style.

00:06:56.640 --> 00:07:02.160
– I promise I will never even think about&nbsp;
going up on a tall building again.

00:07:02.160 --> 00:07:03.520
– Rachel isn’t so lucky.

00:07:04.937 --> 00:07:06.937
(Rachel screaming)

00:07:07.080 --> 00:07:08.080
(thud)

00:07:08.080 --> 00:07:12.080
Jamie cries and begs Rachel to please&nbsp;
“come alive” but Rachel is unresponsive,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:12.080 --> 00:07:16.240
so Jamie is left all alone with Michael coming&nbsp;
down to get her. She runs away screaming for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:16.240 --> 00:07:20.160
help when she is forcefully grabbed&nbsp;
by another terrifying figure: Loomis.

00:07:20.160 --> 00:07:24.880
– What are you doing out here, alone?
– Everybody’s dead! I just want to go home.

00:07:24.880 --> 00:07:29.040
– No, no. You can’t. I’ve just been there.&nbsp;
That’s the first place he’ll look for you.

00:07:29.040 --> 00:07:32.160
– No, we just established that that’s not the&nbsp;
first place he looked for her. Instead,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:32.160 --> 00:07:35.600
he decides to take Jamie to the school.&nbsp;
They break in and Loomis may have one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:35.600 --> 00:07:38.240
of the worst poker faces I’ve ever&nbsp;
seen while trying to comfort her.

00:07:38.240 --> 00:07:42.396
– [Loomis] We’ll hear some sirens, soon.
– [Jamie] And We’ll be safe?

00:07:42.396 --> 00:07:43.436
– Yes.

00:07:44.369 --> 00:07:46.462
– You don't believe that. Do you?

00:07:46.462 --> 00:07:47.360
– NO.

00:07:47.360 --> 00:07:51.200
– Unsurprisingly, Michael Myers breaks in&nbsp;
almost immediately and incapacitates Loomis,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:51.200 --> 00:07:54.240
leaving Jamie trapped in the school. As&nbsp;
she tries to run away she falls down the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:54.240 --> 00:07:57.760
stairs and hurts herself, where Michael is&nbsp;
able to grab her. Rachel suddenly appears,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:57.760 --> 00:08:01.760
alive. This is why you gotta check for a pulse. She&nbsp;
blinds Michael with a fire extinguisher and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:01.760 --> 00:08:05.280
they flee the school to find the protection&nbsp;
of the Illinois boys. Apparently the Sheriff&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:05.280 --> 00:08:08.800
never found them and killing a guy&nbsp;
didn’t deter them from continuing.

00:08:08.800 --> 00:08:11.360
Little do they know, Michael Myers&nbsp;
hitched a ride on the bottom of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:11.360 --> 00:08:14.560
their truck and eventually gets the&nbsp;
driver. All of this results in Jamie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:14.560 --> 00:08:17.520
being turned into a human pinball&nbsp;
between the seat glove compartment

00:08:17.751 --> 00:08:19.440
(pinball game noises)

00:08:19.440 --> 00:08:21.751
...and Rachel taking the wheel to do this.

00:08:21.751 --> 00:08:24.231
(screeching brakes)

00:08:25.920 --> 00:08:26.640
And this.

00:08:27.116 --> 00:08:29.800
– [Homer Simpson] I have road rage and I know how to use it!

00:08:32.240 --> 00:08:34.640
– [Zac] Causing him to fall over into a&nbsp;
roadside ditch as state police&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:34.640 --> 00:08:38.160
arrive. Rachel yells at Jamie to stay in&nbsp;
the car, but she doesn’t. At this point,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:38.160 --> 00:08:41.440
she’s been smashed around a car, so&nbsp;
she might still be a little bit hazy.

00:08:41.440 --> 00:08:44.880
She takes Michael’s hand and has an&nbsp;
expression of trying to understand him.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:44.880 --> 00:08:48.640
I’m sure there are different interpretations of&nbsp;
what exactly transpires between the two here,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:48.640 --> 00:08:53.680
but I’ve always seen it as Michael passing part of&nbsp;
his curse onto her, based on what goes down next.

00:08:53.680 --> 00:08:57.760
Jamie and Rachel return home to Darlene and&nbsp;
Richard. As Darlene is drawing Jamie a bath,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:57.760 --> 00:09:01.280
almost robotically in a manner very&nbsp;
similar to Michael Myers’s behaviour,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:01.280 --> 00:09:06.160
Jamie puts back on the clown mask. She picks up&nbsp;
the scissors from a counter and Darlene screams.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:06.160 --> 00:09:10.400
Only this time, it is revealed to be Jamie who&nbsp;
stabbed her. She stands at the top of the stairs&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:10.400 --> 00:09:15.440
in her clown costume, weapon in hand, just as&nbsp;
Michael did in front of his house back in 1963.

00:09:15.440 --> 00:09:19.440
The same evil that has controlled Michael&nbsp;
all these years has seemingly now affiliated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:19.440 --> 00:09:23.120
Jamie. There is even a point later on where&nbsp;
Loomis implies that Michael “made her do it.”

00:09:23.680 --> 00:09:29.200
– What about your stepmother, Jamie? You love her,  don't you? He made you stab her.

00:09:29.200 --> 00:09:33.040
– ...which kind of implies that he’s referencing&nbsp;
Jamie’s account of what went on that night.

00:09:33.040 --> 00:09:37.840
Jamie develops this connection to Michael Myers.&nbsp;
Dr. Loomis, having been so close to the evil for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:37.840 --> 00:09:41.360
so many years, seems to understand the nature of&nbsp;
what’s going on with her, but from the point of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:41.360 --> 00:09:45.760
view of anyone else, her behaviour would quickly&nbsp;
be diagnosed as a reaction to emotional trauma.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:45.760 --> 00:09:50.080
However, according to The Child Mind Institute,&nbsp;
violent behavior is not a typical reaction to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:50.080 --> 00:09:54.400
childhood trauma. So the most likely scenario is&nbsp;
that her behaviour was attributed to her physical&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:54.400 --> 00:09:58.400
injuries, like when her head SLAMMED against&nbsp;
the glove compartment. According to a study at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:58.400 --> 00:10:01.920
The University of Michigan, “young people&nbsp;
who suffered a recent head injury (within&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:01.920 --> 00:10:05.760
a year of being questioned for the study) were&nbsp;
even more likely to report violent behavior.”

00:10:05.760 --> 00:10:09.920
She also loses the ability to speak, another&nbsp;
parallel shared between her and Michael Myers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:09.920 --> 00:10:14.080
who never spoke again after his childhood&nbsp;
outburst of aggressive behaviour in ‘63. With&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:14.080 --> 00:10:18.480
Jamie seemingly following in her family member’s&nbsp;
footsteps, a bleak future for her looks imminent,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:18.480 --> 00:10:22.000
but one key difference between the two&nbsp;
would send her down a different path.

00:10:22.458 --> 00:10:25.762
(cinematic impact)

00:10:27.810 --> 00:10:31.060
(mysterious music)

00:10:31.520 --> 00:10:35.440
Luckily for Jamie, she is not given the same&nbsp;
treatment that her Mom’s brother was given&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:35.440 --> 00:10:39.760
25 years before. Instead of being shipped out&nbsp;
to Smith’s Grove or another mental facility,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:39.760 --> 00:10:43.120
she gets to stay nearby, and checks&nbsp;
into the Haddonfield Children’s Clinic.

00:10:43.120 --> 00:10:46.000
Over the course of the next year, she&nbsp;
would receive treatment there while also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:46.000 --> 00:10:49.440
going to school with the other patients. She&nbsp;
became close with a boy named Billy Hill,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:49.440 --> 00:10:52.320
who had a bad stutter, causing the two&nbsp;
to bond over their speech issues. It&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:52.320 --> 00:10:55.920
seems like the two have kind of a puppy-love&nbsp;
relationship going on by the next school year.

00:10:55.920 --> 00:10:59.760
– [Tina] Billy is going to have&nbsp;
to fight off a lot of boys.

00:10:59.760 --> 00:11:04.480
– Dr. Loomis takes up the job as her psychiatrist,&nbsp;
which I’m surprised her step-parents were OK with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:04.480 --> 00:11:07.680
given that Loomis nearly tried to shoot&nbsp;
her at one point after realizing she was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:07.680 --> 00:11:11.280
carrying the evil, and she’s also tended&nbsp;
to by other staff members of the clinic.

00:11:11.280 --> 00:11:13.360
Rachel came to visit her regularly and sometimes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:13.360 --> 00:11:15.600
brought her friend Tina to&nbsp;
help keep Jamie company.

00:11:15.600 --> 00:11:19.360
Jamie continues to be haunted by nightmares,&nbsp;
and they appear to have gotten more severe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:19.360 --> 00:11:23.040
causing her to thrash around in her sleep and&nbsp;
relive her attack against her step-mother.

00:11:23.040 --> 00:11:28.240
After one such terror on October 30th 1989, Jamie&nbsp;
woke up trying to scream, but not being able to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:28.240 --> 00:11:32.320
produce any sound. All of the trauma from the&nbsp;
year before has manifested itself in Jamie in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:32.320 --> 00:11:36.560
what’s referred to as “selective mutism.”&nbsp;
According to the Cedars-Sinai Health Library,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:36.560 --> 00:11:40.240
“the main sign of selective mutism is&nbsp;
a month or more of failure to speak&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:40.240 --> 00:11:44.560
only in certain social situations.” The condition&nbsp;
is still being studied today for possible causes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:44.560 --> 00:11:48.080
but researchers have identified a number&nbsp;
of them, one of which is selective mutism&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:48.080 --> 00:11:52.320
as a result of a traumatic experience, which&nbsp;
needless to say, fits Jamie’s case pretty well.

00:11:52.320 --> 00:11:56.080
Another possible factor is poor family&nbsp;
relationships. Jamie’s uncle tried to kill&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:56.080 --> 00:12:00.880
her 3 times, so again, she more than qualifies.&nbsp;
It is also noted that selective mutism can run in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:00.880 --> 00:12:05.040
the family, which could also be relevant because&nbsp;
Michael hasn’t spoken since he was 6 years old.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:05.040 --> 00:12:09.040
In the original timeline there’s a supernatural&nbsp;
reason for this, which seems to apply to both him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:09.040 --> 00:12:12.560
and Jamie in relation to the Curse of Thorn.&nbsp;
There is a difference between them though,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:12.560 --> 00:12:14.960
because Michael doesn’t appear&nbsp;
to really ever attempt to speak,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:14.960 --> 00:12:18.720
and Jamie tries to speak unsuccessfully.&nbsp;
Her willingness to fight back against her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:18.720 --> 00:12:23.120
circumstances may have something to do with why&nbsp;
she has not become a lost cause like Michael has.

00:12:23.120 --> 00:12:26.960
The hereditary explanation for Jamie’s&nbsp;
silence could also help explain this moment,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:26.960 --> 00:12:30.160
where Jamie’s mother seemed to have&nbsp;
a temporary bout of mutism, herself.

00:12:35.078 --> 00:12:36.240
– H-help...

00:12:36.240 --> 00:12:40.240
– Jamie comes to the realization that her newfound&nbsp;
connection to Michael also allows her to see&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:40.240 --> 00:12:44.080
through his eyes. While she can not speak, she&nbsp;
is able to write down, “He’s coming for me.”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:44.080 --> 00:12:48.080
But the orderlies are more concerned about her&nbsp;
intense episode, and this detail is overlooked.

00:12:48.080 --> 00:12:52.560
Hours later, after Jamie is stabilized, she wakes&nbsp;
up to a Halloween morning visit from Rachel, Tina,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:52.560 --> 00:12:55.680
and her doberman pinscher, Max.&nbsp;
Rachel brings her a new costume,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:55.680 --> 00:13:00.400
which Jamie is excited to try out until Dr. Loomis&nbsp;
appears in an almost villainous fashion. Why’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:00.400 --> 00:13:04.320
he always gotta be wearing that jacket, even&nbsp;
when he’s inside and it looks uncomfortable?

00:13:04.320 --> 00:13:08.480
Rachel explains she’s leaving town for a couple&nbsp;
days, but they’re interrupted by a rock smashing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:08.480 --> 00:13:12.880
through Jamie’s window. An attached note reads:&nbsp;
“The Evil Child Must Die.” The public has come&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:12.880 --> 00:13:16.560
to see Jamie as a second coming of Michael&nbsp;
Myers, which adds to her distress and makes her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:16.560 --> 00:13:20.160
unwilling to vent her issues with her doctor,&nbsp;
perhaps out of fear that opening up will make&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:20.160 --> 00:13:24.160
her seem like even more of a freak. It doesn’t&nbsp;
help that Loomis is like a maniac in this one.

00:13:24.319 --> 00:13:26.319
(maniacal laughter)

00:13:26.560 --> 00:13:29.600
That morning during art class, she&nbsp;
visualizes Michael Myers trying to get&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:29.600 --> 00:13:33.280
into her house while Rachel is showering,&nbsp;
and sees Max furiously barking at him.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:33.280 --> 00:13:37.040
She frantically draws a picture of Max, which&nbsp;
Billy notices and communicates to Loomis,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:37.040 --> 00:13:39.200
who calls Rachel and tells&nbsp;
her to get out of the house.

00:13:39.200 --> 00:13:41.840
Once she’s safe, Loomis tries&nbsp;
to assure Jamie that it’s OK,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:41.840 --> 00:13:46.400
but Jamie knows something is still wrong. Loomis&nbsp;
begs her to help communicate with writing.

00:13:46.400 --> 00:13:50.799
– Tell me what you know! Here! Write! Write! Write!&nbsp;

00:13:50.960 --> 00:13:54.560
– He sounds like my YouTube commenters&nbsp;
trying to get me to do a video on Candyman.

00:13:54.560 --> 00:13:56.400
– Write! Write! Write! 

00:13:56.400 --> 00:13:58.640
– This is a lot of responsibility to put on a child,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:58.640 --> 00:14:02.800
and Jamie shuts down. That afternoon, she has&nbsp;
another nightmare with seizure-like symptoms,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:02.800 --> 00:14:05.840
as she sees Michael stabbing her step-sister&nbsp;
to death with a pair of scissors.

00:14:06.068 --> 00:14:09.751
However, because her dream earlier that day did not lead to the police finding Michael Myers, 

00:14:09.751 --> 00:14:12.100
she's kind of unsure if this is real or not.

00:14:12.100 --> 00:14:15.920
In the afternoon, she dreams through Michael’s&nbsp;
eyes again and sees him stalk Tina and her friend&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:15.920 --> 00:14:19.840
Sammy on their way to the clinic to visit her.&nbsp;
As she panics in her sleep, Tina’s boyfriend,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:19.840 --> 00:14:23.840
coincidentally also named Michael, pulls up&nbsp;
and unintentionally saves them just in time.

00:14:23.840 --> 00:14:28.080
But when Jamie wakes up, she knows Michael is out&nbsp;
there and as she struggles to the window, she sees&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:28.080 --> 00:14:32.080
him lurking in the tree outside and freaks&nbsp;
out. She believes he’s chasing her and hides&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:32.080 --> 00:14:35.680
in the basement, only to realize she has been&nbsp;
being followed by the janitor of the facility,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:35.680 --> 00:14:40.400
which is less scary if only slightly. The janitor&nbsp;
doesn’t know sign language, so Jamie’s is sent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:40.400 --> 00:14:44.320
back to bed where Loomis checks on her, once again&nbsp;
looking for answers about where Michael Myers is.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:44.320 --> 00:14:48.467
Their interaction makes me wonder how this man&nbsp;
has ever been permitted to work with children.

00:14:50.560 --> 00:14:58.927
– [Dr. Loomis] Today in the cemetery, somebody dug up a&nbsp;
coffin. It was a coffin of a nine year old girl.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:00.400 --> 00:15:03.600
What do you think he’s going to do with that?

00:15:03.600 --> 00:15:06.400
– Also, I don’t know how Jamie’s&nbsp;
age skipped an entire year from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:06.400 --> 00:15:09.267
seven years old to nine years&nbsp;
old the following Halloween?

00:15:09.267 --> 00:15:12.720
– [Tina] Jamie’s a 9-year-old girl!
– [Loomis] You are nine years old!

00:15:12.720 --> 00:15:15.440
– It’s possible that Tina and Dr.&nbsp;
Loomis were just rounding up;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:15.440 --> 00:15:18.320
like if Jamie was born in November&nbsp;
or December. That way she still would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:18.320 --> 00:15:23.360
have been seven in October 1988, then in&nbsp;
1989 she’d be eight, but about to turn 9.

00:15:23.517 --> 00:15:25.200
So they might refer to her as a 9 year old.

00:15:25.200 --> 00:15:29.120
In the evening, Jamie and Billy participate in a&nbsp;
Halloween pageant put on by the children’s clinic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:29.120 --> 00:15:33.120
and Jamie has yet another episode. She sees&nbsp;
Tina getting into a car with Michael Myers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:33.120 --> 00:15:36.640
and her reaction is so severe that Jamie&nbsp;
nearly throws herself over the railing.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:36.640 --> 00:15:40.160
With the help and patience of Billy, she’s&nbsp;
able to mutter the word “store”. Following&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:40.160 --> 00:15:43.440
a very frustrating game of charades and&nbsp;
a couple more audible clues from Jamie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:43.440 --> 00:15:47.200
Loomis and the Sheriff determine which store&nbsp;
-- a gas station that Tina has stepped into.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:47.200 --> 00:15:49.840
The cops are able to pick her up&nbsp;
and safely bring her to the clinic.

00:15:49.840 --> 00:15:53.600
When Tina arrives, Jamie is able to speak&nbsp;
her name and Tina is thrilled and shocked&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:53.600 --> 00:15:57.280
to see Jamie talking again. This is a big&nbsp;
breakthrough, and lines up with what we know&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:57.280 --> 00:16:01.440
about selective mutism, which can be exacerbated&nbsp;
by stress. It makes sense that Jamie is able to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:01.440 --> 00:16:05.520
speak again after the huge relief of seeing&nbsp;
Tina is OK, and it also makes sense why she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:05.520 --> 00:16:09.280
has difficulty speaking around Dr. Loomis:&nbsp;
the guy’s not exactly putting her at ease.

00:16:09.280 --> 00:16:12.720
However, just because Jamie can talk,&nbsp;
doesn’t mean that the adults around her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:12.720 --> 00:16:16.400
will necessarily listen. As Jamie tries to&nbsp;
tell Tina that she was with The Boogeyman,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:16.400 --> 00:16:20.080
Tina brushes it off and decides to head out&nbsp;
to her Halloween party. This leaves Jamie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:20.080 --> 00:16:24.160
stressed but determined to protect her. As Tina&nbsp;
leaves, Loomis instructs two police officers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:24.160 --> 00:16:27.760
to follow her. Billy overhears where she’s&nbsp;
going and relays this information to Jamie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:27.760 --> 00:16:32.000
so they both sneak out to head toward&nbsp;
the farm where more danger would await.

00:16:32.000 --> 00:16:34.722
(cinematic impact)

00:16:36.861 --> 00:16:38.861
(suspenseful music)

00:16:40.640 --> 00:16:43.920
When Jamie and Billy arrive at The&nbsp;
Tower Farm, Michael Myers has already&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:43.920 --> 00:16:48.290
claimed four victims and is targeting&nbsp;
a fifth in Tina, but Jamie screams out.

00:16:48.396 --> 00:16:49.920
– Leave her alone!

00:16:49.920 --> 00:16:53.760
– This is another important step for Jamie’s&nbsp;
recovery, as she’s now not only able to speak,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:53.760 --> 00:16:58.320
but do so very loudly and in the most stressful&nbsp;
scenario imaginable. Michael diverts his attention&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:58.320 --> 00:17:01.920
onto Jamie and Billy. After Jamie’s quick&nbsp;
cutbacks send Michael crashing into a tree,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:01.920 --> 00:17:05.040
she finds herself unable to find her footing&nbsp;
and it looks like he’s actually going to get&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:05.040 --> 00:17:09.200
her this time until Tina sacrifices herself&nbsp;
to give her young friend a chance to escape.

00:17:09.200 --> 00:17:11.920
Loomis arrives with the police and&nbsp;
asks Jamie if she will now agree to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:11.920 --> 00:17:14.160
help him and she agrees to go along with his plan.

00:17:14.160 --> 00:17:17.760
This involves Loomis using Jamie as bait at&nbsp;
the old Myers’ house, and we’re just supposed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:17.760 --> 00:17:21.040
to ignore the fact that this looks nothing&nbsp;
like the Myers house. In another episode,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:21.040 --> 00:17:24.960
Jamie sees Michael back at the clinic and fears&nbsp;
for Billy’s safety, so the police protecting the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:24.960 --> 00:17:29.040
perimeter outside go back over there to try to&nbsp;
catch Michael. However, Michael sneaks back to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:29.040 --> 00:17:32.800
the house anyway and Jamie witnesses the last&nbsp;
officer left to protect her getting pounded on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:32.800 --> 00:17:37.200
her masked adversary, so she gets out of there and&nbsp;
tries to play a dangerous game of hide-and-seek.

00:17:37.200 --> 00:17:41.280
Michael quickly discovers her in the laundry&nbsp;
chute, so she lets go and rides down it. Let’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:41.280 --> 00:17:45.280
face it, we ALL wanted to do this at some&nbsp;
point as a kid. If you didn’t you’re lame.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:45.280 --> 00:17:47.360
She’s only able to get away by climbing back up,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:47.360 --> 00:17:50.560
then running upstairs where comes&nbsp;
upon the bodies of Max and Rachel.

00:17:50.560 --> 00:17:54.640
Even after everything she’s been through, I’m&nbsp;
tempted to say this was the most traumatic,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:54.640 --> 00:17:58.400
because Rachel was the one person who was there&nbsp;
for her to keep her safe no matter what when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:58.400 --> 00:18:02.560
Michael initially came after her. She also notices&nbsp;
the coffin that Loomis told her about earlier,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:02.560 --> 00:18:05.840
which I just made the connection that that’s&nbsp;
what he was referring to. She climbs inside,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:05.840 --> 00:18:10.080
essentially suggesting she’s going to give herself&nbsp;
up to him, but before he takes her life, she has a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:10.080 --> 00:18:14.320
moment with her uncle, not the empty, faceless&nbsp;
killer, but the rarely seen human side of him.

00:18:16.640 --> 00:18:18.447
– Let me see.

00:18:18.499 --> 00:18:20.499
(heavy breathing)

00:18:23.659 --> 00:18:25.000
You’re just like me.

00:18:25.000 --> 00:18:29.280
This moment of emotionality is cut short&nbsp;
however, when Jamie touches him and the rage&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:29.280 --> 00:18:33.440
consumes him once more. Michael goes berserk&nbsp;
and Jamie just narrowly gets away to retreat&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:33.440 --> 00:18:38.400
to the arms of Dr. Loomis, but to her horror, he&nbsp;
actually picks her up and offers her to Michael.

00:18:38.400 --> 00:18:42.240
– You want her! Here she is. 

00:18:42.240 --> 00:18:46.000
– Loomis is really just using her as bait to&nbsp;
lure Michael into this trap he has set up,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:46.000 --> 00:18:50.000
but as far as I can tell, Jamie was not in&nbsp;
on it. I say that because the panic we see&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:50.000 --> 00:18:54.480
from her seems so genuine. If you think about&nbsp;
it, this is just so immoral on Loomis’s part&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:54.480 --> 00:18:58.720
and probably very damaging for Jamie’s mental&nbsp;
health, if that’s even a thing at this point.

00:18:58.720 --> 00:19:02.640
She just got her voice back a couple of&nbsp;
hours ago. She lost her adoptive sister,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:02.640 --> 00:19:06.480
her dog, and her friend, who gave it&nbsp;
all up to protect her. And now Loomis,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:06.480 --> 00:19:09.600
who she’s literally just learned to trust&nbsp;
for the first time -- and by the way is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:09.600 --> 00:19:14.320
her psychiatrist (!) and is literally supposed to be the one&nbsp;
protecting her from emotional trauma – ends up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:14.320 --> 00:19:17.920
being the one to cause her a great deal&nbsp;
of emotional distress because he is now&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:17.920 --> 00:19:21.280
more obsessed with destroying his former&nbsp;
patient than helping his current one.

00:19:21.280 --> 00:19:24.720
Despite the damage this might have done&nbsp;
Jamie, Michael is captured by the police&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:24.720 --> 00:19:28.480
and taken to jail -- so it seems as if the&nbsp;
whole nightmare may be over for Jamie Lloyd.

00:19:28.480 --> 00:19:31.920
She’s escorted to the back of a police car,&nbsp;
as things are sorted out in the station, when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:31.920 --> 00:19:36.560
suddenly, they hear an explosion inside, which the&nbsp;
cop goes to check one. Jamie gets out of the car,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:36.560 --> 00:19:40.400
directly disobeying what the cop told her, but&nbsp;
whatever, and goes inside to find that the rest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:40.400 --> 00:19:44.720
of the police force has been massacred and Michael&nbsp;
has been broken out of captivity once more.

00:19:45.781 --> 00:19:47.034
– [Jamie] (crying) No...

00:19:48.560 --> 00:19:51.840
– Jamie is not seen again for the next six years.

00:19:51.840 --> 00:19:54.240
– [Tommy] Six years ago, on Halloween night,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:54.240 --> 00:19:59.680
Michael and Jamie vanished. Many people believed&nbsp;
them dead, but I think someone hid them away.

00:19:59.680 --> 00:20:03.440
– This suggests that the man that freed Michael,&nbsp;
who we later find out to be Dr. Terrance Wynn,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:03.440 --> 00:20:07.360
kidnapped her shortly after, and kept her&nbsp;
hidden underground at Smith’s Grove Sanitarium.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:07.360 --> 00:20:11.280
Michael’s human sacrifices are tied to the&nbsp;
curse placed on him by The Cult of Thorn.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:11.280 --> 00:20:14.480
As a result, he only appears when the&nbsp;
Thorn constellation can be seen in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:14.480 --> 00:20:17.920
sky, and that doesn’t happen&nbsp;
again until October of 1995.

00:20:17.920 --> 00:20:22.080
It is not clear how she became pregnant. There&nbsp;
are a lot of theories, but I don’t think any&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:22.080 --> 00:20:26.320
of them can be proven, and none of them seem&nbsp;
to involve Jamie getting pregnant by choice,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:26.320 --> 00:20:29.280
so since there’s nothing for me to&nbsp;
analyze here, let’s just move on.

00:20:29.280 --> 00:20:34.160
On October 30th, 1995, Jamie gave birth to&nbsp;
her son, who would later be named Stephen.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:34.160 --> 00:20:35.920
The cult takes the baby away from her, but&nbsp;
midwife who assisted with the delivery is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:35.920 --> 00:20:39.600
secretly on her side and makes an effort to&nbsp;
help her escape the sanitarium with her son.

00:20:39.600 --> 00:20:41.520
This is presumably the first time she’s gotten out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:41.520 --> 00:20:44.080
in public since she was a little&nbsp;
kid, but unfortunately for her,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:44.080 --> 00:20:48.080
she is not the only one who is unleashed&nbsp;
that night. Michael is sent to go after her.

00:20:48.080 --> 00:20:51.200
She makes her way to an empty bus&nbsp;
station. Unable to get through to police,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:51.200 --> 00:20:54.640
she does the next best thing and calls&nbsp;
into a radio show, which is discussing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:54.640 --> 00:20:57.360
Haddonfield and Michael Myers, seeing&nbsp;
as this is the day before Halloween.

00:20:59.086 --> 00:21:00.773
– [Jamie] It’s&nbsp;Michael. 

00:21:00.773 --> 00:21:05.680
Michael Myers. Look, someone, anyone,&nbsp;
help me. Dr. Loomis are you out there? Can you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:05.680 --> 00:21:08.240
hear me Dr. Loomis, I need your help.
– [Barry] Please, please, no, no stop&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:08.240 --> 00:21:10.480
this. What the hell is going on tonight?&nbsp;

00:21:10.480 --> 00:21:13.920
– Knowing that Michael is not far behind&nbsp;
her, she hides the baby in a bathroom&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:13.920 --> 00:21:18.000
and gets as far away as possible in order to&nbsp;
lure Michael away from the baby. She ends up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:18.000 --> 00:21:21.040
getting run off the road near a farm&nbsp;
and tries to hide inside of the barn.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:21.040 --> 00:21:24.560
As she looks for another hiding spot, she&nbsp;
realizes that Michael is looking for her.

00:21:24.560 --> 00:21:28.400
Under normal circumstances, Jamie probably&nbsp;
would have run away on foot again, but this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:28.400 --> 00:21:32.160
time things are different, because she just&nbsp;
gave birth no more than a couple of hours ago.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:32.160 --> 00:21:36.400
Usually a woman is confined to a couple of days of&nbsp;
bedrest after giving birth, so the fact that she’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:36.400 --> 00:21:40.560
even able to be on her feet and moving around&nbsp;
is probably a result of motherly adrenaline.

00:21:40.560 --> 00:21:44.640
Adrenaline comes from the hormone epinephrine
in our brains produced to increase the blood flow&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:44.640 --> 00:21:48.320
to our muscles and heart rate. When you&nbsp;
hear about a fight-or-flight response in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:48.320 --> 00:21:51.760
humans or in animals, that’s adrenaline&nbsp;
kicking in to try to save our lives.

00:21:51.760 --> 00:21:56.320
It’s thought that a mother possesses a survival&nbsp;
instinct not only for her, but also for her child,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:56.320 --> 00:21:59.920
sometimes drawing extra strength&nbsp;
that she does not seem to otherwise possess.

00:21:59.920 --> 00:22:03.520
Jamie seems to use this strength to push&nbsp;
her through the post delivery exhaustion,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:03.520 --> 00:22:06.800
hide her baby lure Michael as&nbsp;
far away as possible. But now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:06.800 --> 00:22:10.695
her body can take her no further, and&nbsp;
Haddonfield’s boogeyman catches up with her.

00:22:12.303 --> 00:22:14.303
(stinger)

00:22:15.112 --> 00:22:16.640
(choking sounds)

00:22:16.640 --> 00:22:20.240
As she is impaled on… apparently this&nbsp;
thing is a corn thresher... she tries&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:20.240 --> 00:22:24.480
to reach out to Michael the same way that she did&nbsp;
as a child but this time, gets no sympathy.

00:22:24.480 --> 00:22:28.400
The last thing she says is, “you can’t have&nbsp;
the baby Michael,” and realizing that she’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:28.400 --> 00:22:32.320
no longer useful to him, he turns on&nbsp;
the machine to rip apart her insides.

00:22:32.320 --> 00:22:35.760
Jamie Lloyd’s story is a tragic&nbsp;
one. At only seven years old,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:35.760 --> 00:22:39.280
her life completely changed when she lost&nbsp;
her parents, was attacked by her uncle,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:39.280 --> 00:22:43.360
and developed stress related speech issues as&nbsp;
she watched nearly everyone close to her die.

00:22:43.360 --> 00:22:48.000
But if there is one silver lining, one takeaway&nbsp;
about her character, it’s that she found herself&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:48.000 --> 00:22:52.000
in exactly the same scenario as Michael&nbsp;
Myers, but didn’t follow in his footsteps&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:52.000 --> 00:22:56.000
to become Haddonfield’s next boogeyman. As&nbsp;
difficult as it may have been, she recovered,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:56.000 --> 00:23:00.560
and refused to succumb to the evil, even using her&nbsp;
connection to Michael as an advantage against him.

00:23:00.560 --> 00:23:03.680
But I guess if there’s a lesson to be&nbsp;
learned here, it’s that Loomis should&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:03.680 --> 00:23:07.600
never work with children. To see my lessons&nbsp;
on Loomis and other Halloween characters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:07.600 --> 00:23:11.360
click that playlist on the left. Let me know who&nbsp;
else you’d like to see covered here on Horror&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:11.360 --> 00:23:16.000
History and remember to subscribe to CZsWorld&nbsp;
for new horrors every week, ring that deathbell&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:16.000 --> 00:23:21.365
and make sure you select ALL notifications. I will&nbsp;
